{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>As He spoke to you.</b> And where did He speak? (Deuteronomy 28) ״בָּרוּךְ אַתָּה בָּעִיר״ (Sifrei)." "<b>You shall lend.</b> Every term of lending, when it falls upon the lender, falls in the causative/active voice — for example, וְהִלְוִיתָ, וְהַעֲבַטְתָּ. And if it had said וְעָבַטְתָּ, it would have fallen upon the borrower — like וְלָוִיתָ." "<b>You shall lend to nations.</b> Might one say you would be borrowing from this one and lending to that one? Scripture says: ״וְאַתָּה לֹא תַעֲבֹט״." "<b>And you shall rule over many nations.</b> Might one say other nations would rule over you? Scripture says: ״וּבְךָ לֹא יִמְשֹׁלוּ״ (ibid.)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:47:11.742366375Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}